  "result": "`Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line, and all 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` compared the SKU you pass in against each line's item **name** (`l.item.name != sku`), not its SKU. `'sku-1'` never matches `'Widget'`, so nothing was ever removed. `Cart.add` already matches on `item.sku`, so `remove` was the odd one out.\n\n**Fix:** a one-word change, `l.item.name` \u2192 `l.item.sku`.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1` (only the Gadget is left). Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.\n\nNone of the existing tests call `Cart.remove`, which is how this got through. Want me to add a regression test for it?",
